Spawn, objective 234 [recoverability][observability] (the lead's follow-up to the stray integrator 2375721, sync/incident-2375721-rev-b.md, assigned 2026-11-19 15:35; author rev-i; readers rev-j first, rev-k second): each `spawn integrate` start that takes the lock records who it is, so the next stray is named from the store.

Why. On 2026-11-18 14:57-15:03 a stray `spawn integrate` (pid 2375721) judged with the live database for at least an hour. It halted mission 9. rev-b's read-only search (journal, every transcript, scopes, scenarios, deploy, peers' scripts, shell history) closed it "starter unknown": no store record names an integrator's start or pid. Objective 221 now refuses a second integrator; this names the one that holds the lock.

What changes (crates/spawn-cli/src/integrate.rs, crates/spawn-postgres/sql/schema.sql):
- Right after the integrator takes its lock (objective 221), on the lock's connection and before anything else is written, it records one control record `integrator.started`, with exactly these fields:
  - `pid`, `ppid`;
  - `parent_comm`: /proc/<ppid>/comm, or null;
  - `ancestors`: [{pid, comm}] from the parent up to pid 1, at most 16; an ancestor that cannot be read ends the list;
  - `cwd`: the working directory, or null;
  - `cgroup`: the unified line of /proc/self/cgroup ("0::<path>"), which names the unit or scope (spawn-integrate.service, a terminal's scope, a guarded scope), or null;
  - `gate`: the gate script, absolute;
  - `gate_from_env`: whether SPAWN_GATE named it (false: its default, read from cwd);
  - `root`: absolute;
  - `once`: `--once`.
- On stdout: "integrate: started as pid <pid> by <parent comm> (pid <ppid>) in <cwd>, cgroup <cgroup>; gate <gate> (from SPAWN_GATE | SPAWN_GATE unset: the default, read from the working directory)". Unknown values print as "unknown".
- If the store refuses the record, stderr says "integrate: cannot record integrator.started: <error>" and the start goes on: the lock keeps a second integrator out, not the record.
- A start the gate check or the lock refuses records nothing, as now.
- Store (spawn_integrator_record, owner only): the type is allowed and its shape checked, each field alone (SQLSTATE 22023):
  - pid a number >= 1, ppid a number >= 0;
  - gate and root non-empty strings;
  - gate_from_env and once booleans;
  - parent_comm, cwd and cgroup strings or null (present);
  - ancestors an array of {pid number, comm string}.
  - Values are never checked. The record is folded into no table (spawn_control_apply: null).
- docs/fleet-architecture.md says it in the integrator paragraph.

What stays as it is: the lock and its refusals (221), every other record kind, the passes. Nothing is read on any polled path; one write per start.

Files: crates/spawn-cli/src/integrate.rs, crates/spawn-postgres/sql/schema.sql, docs/fleet-architecture.md; tests in crates/spawn-cli/src/integrate/tests.rs and crates/spawn-cli/src/integrate/database_tests.rs. Owner files: rsi/scenarios/234.sh, rsi/backlog/234.json.

Acceptance: rsi/scenarios/234.sh. Black box, on a database of its own, no missions. Each integrator is started by a copy of sh named "st) 1 (234", which runs it as a child, so the parent's pid and comm are known. The name holds ") 1 (": a stat read by the first ")" takes a wrong parent and ends the ancestors there.
- (1) A is started by hand in $WORK/here with SPAWN_GATE unset (a stub scripts/rsi/gate.sh there) and --root ws-a. Within 30 s, one integrator.started is recorded with exactly the fields above:
  - pid = A; ppid = its starter; parent_comm "st) 1 (234";
  - ancestors start [starter, the scenario's shell] and end at pid 1 (or are 16 long);
  - cwd $WORK/here; cgroup the scenario's own unified line (null if it has none);
  - gate $WORK/here/scripts/rsi/gate.sh, gate_from_env false;
  - root $WORK/here/ws-a, once false.
  - A's stdout holds the started line with those values.
- (2) B starts while A runs: refused (exit 1), and there is still one integrator.started.
- (3) A is stopped. C runs --once with SPAWN_GATE=$WORK/gate.sh and exits 0. A second record: pid = C, ppid its starter, gate $WORK/gate.sh, gate_from_env true, once true, root $WORK/ic, cwd $WORK; the stdout line ends "(from SPAWN_GATE)".
- (4) The store refuses integrator.started (the scenario's database wraps spawn_integrator_record to raise on it). D, --once, still exits 0; its stderr says "integrate: cannot record integrator.started: ..."; no record is added.
- (5, rev-k's R1 F1 and F2) E, --once, with SPAWN_GATE set but empty, is started under 18 nested sh. Its record (the third) has:
  - gate $WORK/here/scripts/rsi/gate.sh and gate_from_env false (an empty value names nothing);
  - ancestors[0] = its ppid, and exactly 16 ancestors.
On live main bde44342, 234.sh exits 1 at (1): no integrator.started is recorded.

Tests:
- Unit (integrate/tests.rs, a fake /proc):
  - the record names the process, the parent's comm, the ancestors up to pid 1 (a comm holding ")" read by the last ")"), the unified cgroup line after a v1 line, and the start's own fields;
  - what cannot be read is null (no comm, no cgroup, a v1-only cgroup); a missing stat or ancestor ends the list; the list stops at 16;
  - the stdout line in both SPAWN_GATE forms.
- Store (database_tests.rs): the full record and an all-null one are taken and read back as written; each field's bad shape or absence is refused alone.
- No test is renamed or dropped.

Verified by: after landing and the deploy, the unit's integrator's start shows in the store as an integrator.started with pid = the unit's MainPID, cgroup .../spawn-integrate.service, gate_from_env true (the lead reads it read-only). The journal holds its started line.
